        "original_id": "2ef10598-2f16-5118-b829-512c3eedc41b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Ilysiakos B.C.\n- People: Antonis Fotsis\n- Places: Ilissia\n- Concepts: Elysium, Greek alphabet, Phoenician alphabet\n- Topics: club naming, logo lettering, basketball\n\nFacts:\n- The Phoenician alphabet preceded the Greek alphabet.\n- The Greek alphabet was derived from the Phoenician alphabet.\n- The Greek alphabet was the first alphabetic script with distinct letters for both vowels and consonants.\n- Antonis Fotsis was born on April 2, 1981.\n- Antonis Fotsis is a Greek professional basketball player.\n- Antonis Fotsis has an alternate spelling of his name as Antonios.\n- Antonis Fotsis plays for Ilysiakos.\n- Ilysiakos B.C. is based in Ilissia.\n- Ilysiakos B.C.'s name is said to reference Elysium.\n- Ilysiakos B.C.'s name and logo begin with the Greek letter Η instead of Ι.\n- Ilissia begins with the Greek letter Ι.",
